00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:03.533
Unit eleven. Saving My Work!

2
00:00:04.477 --> 00:00:09.533
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.583 --> 00:00:13.404
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:17.293
Today we learn about Saving My Work. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:22.067
Save. Say it with me. Save!

6
00:00:25.496 --> 00:00:29.296
File. Say it with me. File!

7
00:00:32.827 --> 00:00:36.344
Folder. Say it with me. Folder!

8
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:43.330
Keep. Say it with me. Keep!

9
00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:50.821
Document. Say it with me. Document!

10
00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:57.699
Button. Say it with me. Button!

11
00:01:01.247 --> 00:01:05.413
Remember. Say it with me. Remember!

12
00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:12.970
Store. Say it with me. Store!

13
00:01:16.415 --> 00:01:24.009
Saving my work means the computer will keep and remember it. I click the save button so my file is stored in a folder.

14
00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:27.311
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:28.066 --> 00:01:33.434
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:33.484 --> 00:01:34.634
Folder!

17
00:01:35.536 --> 00:01:41.003
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:41.053 --> 00:01:42.203
Remember!

19
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:48.724
Did you know? If you don't save your work, it might disappear when you turn off the computer!

20
00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:50.793
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:52.087 --> 00:02:00.946
Think and answer. Why is it important to save your work on a computer?

22
00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:02.146
Great answer!

23
00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:08.672
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:08.722 --> 00:02:11.912
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

